  "notes": [
   "The same work twice. A branch adds a retry budget, a policy and a doc page and is left where it is; the same three changes are then made again on `main` with different parents and different SHAs, and the original branch is merged anyway — which brings nothing, because `main` already has the bytes. Both lineages are reachable, which is the state a repository is really in after a force-push, and the state a history walk double-counts unless it compares content rather than ids."
